<title>GERMANY: German union drops UPS sympathy strike plan.</title>
<headline>German union drops UPS sympathy strike plan.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German transport union OeTV said it has dropped plans for solidarity actions in Germany this week following the agreement between United Parcel Service of America and the Teamsters union.</p>
<p>OeTV secretary Heinz Luksch said strikes in support of the Teamsters union had been planned for Orly airport and locations in the Netherlands and Germany.</p>
<p>He told Reuters: &quot;The actions will now not be carried out following the agreement (between UPS and the Teamsters).&quot;</p>
<p>In a union statement, OeTV deputy chairman Wolfgang Warburg congratulated the Teamsters on the deal with UPS and said additional pressure had been put on UPS by international union support for the strike.</p>
